From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <pkgdemonteam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:45:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dlmalloc: check segment_holding's result in sys_trim

Upstream libffi commit 4639c933 ("add NULL check in sys_trim", #966,
libffi 3.6.0).

segment_holding returns NULL when the top chunk lies in no known
segment, which only happens once the closure heap is corrupt; sys_trim
then dereferenced it. Report the corruption through
CORRUPTION_ERROR_ACTION (abort) instead of a wild read.
---
 src/dlmalloc.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/dlmalloc.c b/src/dlmalloc.c
index 1aba657..89d1248 100644
--- a/src/dlmalloc.c
+++ b/src/dlmalloc.c
@@ -3669,6 +3669,8 @@ static int sys_trim(mstate m, size_t pad) {
                       SIZE_T_ONE) * unit;
       msegmentptr sp = segment_holding(m, (char*)m->top);
 
+      if (sp == 0)
+        CORRUPTION_ERROR_ACTION(m);
       if (!is_extern_segment(sp)) {
         if (is_mmapped_segment(sp)) {
           if (HAVE_MMAP &&
